  "prefLabel": "Bcr 103.02 Duties of the Board",
  "priorExpiration": "2003-03-13",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bcr 103.02 Duties of the Board.\n\n(a) The responsibilities of the board include:\n\n(1) Adopting rules to update or change the state building code for codes described in RSA 155-A:1, IV;\n\n(2) Adopting rules relative to procedures of the board’s operation and appeals to the board;\n\n(3) Hearing appeals of variances or exceptions to the state fire code that have been granted or denied by the state fire marshal;\n\n(4) Hearing appeals of decisions of the state fire marshal in enforcing provisions of the state building code, pursuant to RSA 155-A:7, 1;\n\n(5) Reviewing and assessing the application of the state building code and recommending legislation to modify the requirements of the state building code and the state fire code; and\n\n(6) Reviewing the National Fire Protection Association building code and its companion manuals, and any other building codes in order to evaluate whether the state should continue with the International Building Codes and its manuals, switch to other codes, or adopt a combination of codes.\n\nSource. #7760, INTERIM, eff 9-14-02, EXPIRED: 3-13-03\n\nNew. #8003, eff 12-12-03",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bcr100.html"
